  m_Name: GearPumpData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Gear Pump
  engineDescription: "A Gear Pump is a positive displacement pump used to transfer
    liquids by trapping fluid between the rotating gear teeth and the pump casing,
    then forcing it from the inlet to the outlet under pressure. It operates using
    two meshing gears\u2014typically a driving gear and a driven gear\u2014that rotate
    within a closely fitted housing to create a continuous flow of fluid. Its main
    components include the pump casing, driving gear, driven gear, drive shaft, bearings,
    seals, inlet port, and outlet port. During operation, the rotating gears create
    a vacuum at the inlet, drawing fluid into the spaces between the gear teeth and
    the casing. The fluid is carried around the outer circumference of the gears
    and discharged through the outlet as the gear teeth mesh together, preventing
    backflow and maintaining a steady flow rate.\n\nGear pumps are widely used in
    hydraulic systems, lubrication systems, chemical processing, fuel transfer, food
    processing, and industrial fluid handling applications due to their simple construction,
    reliable operation, and ability to handle high-viscosity fluids."
  engineCategory: Engineering
